Cormac McCarthy's last two books, done as one thing. Stella Maris and The Passenger, as one movie seems very, very much something would be wonderful for. 

&#x200B;

I always see Nolan having a focus on internal/introspective characters. Ellroy's characters have, like, zero introspection at all (and I really, really like Ellroy). Villenneuve or...Lynne Ramsay would be interesting for American Tabloid.
